# Teleprompter V2

Standalone band/live karaoke teleprompter with lyrics, chords, BPM sync, and MIDI clock input.

## Features

- **ChordPro format** (.cho/.pro) — industry standard, human-readable
- **Large, high-contrast lyrics display** — dark mode default, chord highlighting
- **BPM-synced auto-scroll** — configurable lines-per-beat
- **Tap tempo** — SPACE to tap, calculates BPM
- **Visual click flash** — screen flashes on downbeat
- **MIDI clock input** — sync BPM from Akai Force, lightrig, or any MIDI clock source
- **Section navigation** — jump between Verse/Chorus/Bridge
- **Transpose** — shift chords up/down semitones ([ / ])
- **Setlist management** — drag-reorder, request queue, song status
- **Song library** — cached scanning, search by title/artist
- **Cross-platform** — runs on Mac, Linux, Raspberry Pi 3B+

## Quick Start

```bash
cd ~/Documents/projects/teleprompter-v2
pip install -e .
python run.py
```

## Controls

| Key | Action |
|-----|--------|
| `F1` | Setlist tab |
| `F2` | Lyrics tab |
| `F3` | BPM tab |
| `F4` | Settings tab |
| `↑/↓` | Scroll lyrics |
| `PgUp/PgDn` | Page scroll |
| `Home/End` | Jump to top/bottom |
| `SPACE` | Tap tempo (BPM tab) / Toggle auto-scroll (Lyrics tab) |
| `t` | Toggle chord display |
| `[` / `]` | Transpose down/up |
| `a` | Add song to setlist |
| `Delete` | Remove song from setlist |
| `Enter` | Select song / Add from search |
| `Escape` | Cancel search |
| `Ctrl+S` | Save setlist |
| `Ctrl+O` | Load setlist |
| `Ctrl+Q` | Quit |

## MIDI Clock Sync

The app listens for MIDI Clock (0xF8) messages to auto-detect BPM and play/stop state.

1. Connect your MIDI source (Akai Force USB, lightrig MIDI out, etc.)
2. In Settings (F4), enter the MIDI port name (partial match works)
3. Click "Scan MIDI Ports" to see available ports
4. Save settings — MIDI sync activates automatically

When MIDI clock is received:
- BPM updates in real-time
- Auto-scroll starts/stops with MIDI Start/Stop
- Lyrics view follows the beat

## Song Format (ChordPro)

```chordpro
{title: Song Title}
{artist: Artist Name}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{time: 4/4}
{capo: 2}

{section: Verse 1}
This is a [G]line with [C]inline [D]chords

{section: Chorus}
[G]Chord [C]on [D]its [G]own
```

### Supported Directives

| Directive | Aliases | Description |
|-----------|---------|-------------|
| `title` | `t` | Song title |
| `artist` | `a` | Artist name |
| `key` | `k` | Musical key |
| `tempo` | `bpm` | BPM |
| `time` | `time_signature` | Time signature |
| `capo` | | Capo fret |
| `section` | `soc`, `chorus` | Section marker |
| `end_of_section` | `eoc`, `eos` | End section |
| `comment` | `c` | Comment line |

## Project Structure

```
teleprompter-v2/
├── run.py                 # Entry point
├── pyproject.toml         # Dependencies
├── config.json            # App config (auto-generated)
├── songs/                 # ChordPro files (.cho/.pro)
├── setlists/              # Saved setlists (.json)
├── src/teleprompter/
│   ├── __init__.py
│   ├── app.py             # Main Textual TUI app
│   ├── chordpro.py        # ChordPro parser/renderer
│   ├── library.py         # Song library & setlist management
│   ├── midi_clock.py      # MIDI clock input handler
│   └── models.py          # Data models
└── tests/                 # Unit tests
```

## Raspberry Pi 3B Deployment

```bash
# On Pi
sudo apt update && sudo apt install python3.11 python3.11-venv libasound2-dev
git clone <repo> teleprompter-v2
cd teleprompter-v2
python3.11 -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate
pip install -e .

# Run
python run.py

# For kiosk mode (auto-start on boot):
# Create systemd service or add to ~/.bashrc
```

## Configuration

`config.json` (auto-generated on first run):

```json
{
  "font_size": 28,
  "line_spacing": 1.4,
  "chord_color": "cyan",
  "text_color": "white",
  "bg_color": "black",
  "highlight_color": "yellow",
  "section_color": "magenta",
  "auto_scroll_enabled": true,
  "scroll_speed_factor": 0.5,
  "scroll_smoothing": true,
  "bpm": 120,
  "time_signature": "4/4",
  "visual_click": true,
  "click_flash_duration_ms": 100,
  "midi_input_port": "",
  "midi_channel": 0,
  "midi_sync_enabled": true,
  "songs_dir": "songs",
  "setlists_dir": "setlists",
  "config_file": "config.json",
  "fullscreen": true,
  "stay_on_top": true
}
```

## Development

```bash
# Install dev dependencies
pip install -e ".[dev]"

# Run tests
pytest

# Lint
ruff check .

# Type check
mypy src/
```

## Integration with lightrig

The teleprompter and lightrig can sync via MIDI clock:

- **lightrig** sends MIDI clock (from Akai Force or internal) → virtual MIDI port
- **teleprompter** receives on virtual MIDI port → auto BPM, auto-scroll sync
- Both stay perfectly in time without network dependency

